WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.838
This one is a proposal,
and it's labeled that way.

2
00:00:02.838 --> 00:00:07.784
Put a well-tuned edge on a flat network
and its value is capped: its identity

3
00:00:07.784 --> 00:00:12.812
signals have nowhere to land, and a
hijacked session inherits all the trust.

4
00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:17.388
The proposal treats the path like
a token: leased for one purpose and

5
00:00:17.388 --> 00:00:21.800
expiring with it, so a flow with no
token behind it shows up as drift.

6
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.238
It's careful about lane discipline, too.

7
00:00:24.238 --> 00:00:29.126
The program observes and records; it
doesn't route packets or pick a vendor.

8
00:00:29.126 --> 00:00:32.040
But one part applies
right now: the evidence.
